+# VCF 9.1 architecture research record
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14. These live sources were consulted independently of the checked-in grading snapshot.
+
+| Published source | URL | Decision informed |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Broadcom Product Interoperability Matrix | https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Interoperability | Cross-checked the VCF 9.1 family selection and the need to treat the VCF bill of materials as one compatible component combination. |
+| Broadcom Compatibility Guide | https://compatibilityguide.broadcom.com/ | Cross-checked that host hardware, I/O devices, and vSAN witness deployment compatibility are separate production readiness checks from product interoperability. |
+| Broadcom KB 440630, “Upgrade Sequence and Related Issues for VMware Cloud Foundation and vSphere Foundation 9.1” | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html | Informed the 9.0.2-to-9.1 path, Operations-first gate, mandatory Management Services address reservation, vIDB consolidation, and Fleet Management Appliance retirement. |
+| Broadcom KB 390634, “Update Sequence for VCF 9.0 and Compatible VMware Products” | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390634/update-sequence-for-vcf-90-and-compatibl.html | Informed the core SDDC ordering constraints: SDDC Manager, NSX, vCenter, vSAN witness, then ESX. |
+
+The live pages can change. `testdata/compatibility-snapshot.json` remains the reproducible implementation authority for this repository, while this record preserves the live research provenance used for the design.
